    "- **LOSS (23000 files)**: fszero one-shot (516ms) is 13.7x slower than cold-ish `git status` (38ms) as a raw change-detection CLI \u2014 even though the one-shot also rebuilds the index for the changed files, the CLI-shaped comparison is a loss.",
    "- **LOSS (23000 files)**: fszero one-shot (516ms) is 13.8x slower than warm `git status` (37ms) as a raw change-detection CLI \u2014 even though the one-shot also rebuilds the index for the changed files, the CLI-shaped comparison is a loss.",
    "- **LOSS (23000 files)**: fszero's detection-only floor (no-change one-shot, 410ms) is 11.0x slower than warm `git status` (37ms): process spawn + store open + full walk dominate.",
    "- **LOSS to watchman (23000 files)**: a settled watchman since-query (12.1ms) beats both git warm status (37ms) and fszero's one-shot floor (410ms). A long-lived daemon with an in-memory view wins the pure detection race; fszero only matches this shape in server mode (see event latency).",
    "- **LOSS (23000 files)**: end-to-end watch latency 2751.3ms (fszero server) vs 11.7ms (watchman) under the identical poll loop \u2014 watchman reports the change faster; fszero is also reindexing before it answers.",
